The lifecycle and pytest fixture design references shibukawa/pgmem,
Copyright (c) 2026 Yoshiki Shibukawa, MIT License. Its notice is included.
The project also takes inspiration from pg-mem and PGlite's testing experience;
their database implementations are not included in the mariamem Python code.

The native bundle uses Wasmer headless and the Go runtime. Their upstream
licenses and the licenses of embedded dependencies must be retained.
Wasmer 7.4.2 headless includes Singlepass under Business Source License 1.1,
not MIT. Its non-production grant, conditional production-use grant, and change
date/license are reproduced in licenses/Wasmer-Singlepass-BUSL-1.1.txt.
See licenses/Wasmer-ATTRIBUTIONS.txt and licenses/Wasmer-Rust-NOTICES.txt
for upstream attributions and collected dependency terms. webc 12.0.1 declares
MIT in its package metadata; a separate upstream license/copyright file is
unavailable. Its exact source/version/hash is recorded without inferred copyright
wording. Runtime notice inventories are reviewed for the pinned macOS arm64
and Ubuntu 24.04 x86_64 distributions. Each new candidate must match its
applicable runtime/source/notice identities and pass separate clean-platform
acceptance; historical approval applies only to its recorded artifact hashes.

The native distribution is intended for testing. Prepared authentication keys
are public, non-secret test material, never production credentials. Exact
source, notice and platform verification remains required for every release
before public distribution. See docs/releasing.md and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

